1
00:00:09,160 --> 00:00:11,840
You said you hadn't seen this tricycle,

2
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:13,480
right?

3
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:16,600
You lied.

4
00:00:17,880 --> 00:00:18,840
Why did you lie?

5
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:22,290
Let me speak for her.

6
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:25,600
This tricycle

7
00:00:26,440 --> 00:00:28,240
holds a special meaning for her.

8
00:00:29,160 --> 00:00:30,480
Before she was born,

9
00:00:30,920 --> 00:00:33,250
her grandfather helped get this tricycle

10
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:35,360
for her father, Gao Yuhai, to run errands

11
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:36,820
and transport materials.

12
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:38,260
A few months later,

13
00:00:38,760 --> 00:00:40,620
her mother died in childbirth...

14
00:00:42,320 --> 00:00:43,380
So her grandfather

15
00:00:43,760 --> 00:00:45,420
took his anger out on Gao Yuhai

16
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:48,250
and took the tricycle back
in a fit of rage.

17
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:50,520
And then?

18
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:53,360
Later, Yayan told me this story.

19
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:56,080
I thought the tricycle
was really worth keeping,

20
00:00:56,080 --> 00:00:57,440
so I asked where it was.

21
00:00:57,560 --> 00:00:59,160
She said it was with her grandparents.

22
00:00:59,160 --> 00:01:00,760
So I found a way to get it back.

23
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:02,840
After you got it back,

24
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:03,960
where did you put it?

25
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:05,840
I put it in the courtyard I rented.

26
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:08,039
But later, it was

27
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:09,840
in the way for several days.

28
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:12,440
It almost scratched
her phone case a few times.

29
00:01:12,520 --> 00:01:14,680
Yayan told me to get rid of it quickly.

30
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:20,760
Haven't changed it yet.

31
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:21,320
It's right here,

32
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:22,280
quite obvious.

33
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:30,920
Okay, let's leave it at that.

34
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:31,600
Bye.

35
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:41,720
Yanfei,

36
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:43,440
Yanfei!

37
00:01:45,520 --> 00:01:46,680
Didn't I tell you

38
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:48,080
to get rid of this tricycle
a couple of days ago?

39
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:49,210
Why is it still here?

40
00:01:49,360 --> 00:01:50,200
What's wrong? Did you bump into it again?

41
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:51,280
Let me see. Are you okay?

42
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:52,640
No, my phone.

43
00:01:53,240 --> 00:01:54,100
Oh, your phone.

44
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:56,200
We can't even drive it,

45
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:58,280
and there are so many actors
walking back and forth.

46
00:01:58,280 --> 00:02:00,610
Mainly, I just really
don't want to see it.

47
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:04,880
Then

48
00:02:05,040 --> 00:02:06,700
I'll take care of it tomorrow.

49
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:08,720
Where are you going to put it?

50
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:10,320
See?

51
00:02:10,639 --> 00:02:12,640
You still care about this tricycle.

52
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:14,240
What do I care?

53
00:02:14,520 --> 00:02:15,560
Put it wherever you want,

54
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:16,400
just not here.

55
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:17,120
Okay.

56
00:02:18,079 --> 00:02:20,480
I just choreographed a really great dance.

57
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:28,280
And then?

58
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:30,400
Where exactly did you leave the car?

59
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:31,800
By the road near the old house.

60
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:34,060
You left it by the road
near the old house?

61
00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:38,160
Not by the road.

62
00:02:38,480 --> 00:02:39,480
It was

63
00:02:39,640 --> 00:02:41,440
at the entrance of the old house.

64
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:43,120
Because Yayan kept telling me
to deal with it.

65
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:44,600
I didn't know where to put it.

66
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:47,329
I couldn't just send it back
to the grandparents.

67
00:02:48,120 --> 00:02:50,079
So I left it

68
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:51,520
at the entrance of her old house.

69
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:52,120
Because I knew

70
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:53,000
Gao Yuhai goes

71
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:54,840
to pay respects
to her mother every Saturday.

72
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:56,400
So I parked it there,

73
00:02:56,680 --> 00:02:58,600
returning it to its rightful owner.

74
00:02:58,600 --> 00:02:59,640
After that,

75
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:00,720
I don't know anything.

76
00:03:00,720 --> 00:03:01,320
No, no.

77
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:02,480
No.

78
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:07,200
You left it at the entrance
of the old house,

79
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:07,600
right?

80
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:09,760
Not

81
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:13,960
by the tree at the intersection
where the accident happened?

82
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:15,360
That's right.

83
00:03:15,760 --> 00:03:16,600
Exact time?

84
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:19,730
About three or four days

85
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:21,240
before the accident.

86
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:02,400
License plate C-B6666.

87
00:04:18,079 --> 00:04:18,740
Captain Li.

88
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:20,519
Thanks.

89
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:33,020
Captain Li,

90
00:04:33,080 --> 00:04:34,680
do you also feel

91
00:04:34,960 --> 00:04:36,760
something is off here? 45509.

92
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:41,360
Everything seems perfectly logical.

93
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:43,159
But within that logic,

94
00:04:43,159 --> 00:04:44,760
something feels illogical.

95
00:04:44,960 --> 00:04:45,760
Yeah.

96
00:04:46,080 --> 00:04:46,920
For example,

97
00:04:47,240 --> 00:04:49,320
why would Song Yanfei

98
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:50,480
take a broken,

99
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:52,159
30-year-old tricycle

100
00:04:52,159 --> 00:04:54,200
from Gao Yayan's grandparents' house?

101
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:54,600
Go on.

102
00:04:54,880 --> 00:04:55,320
Also,

103
00:04:55,480 --> 00:04:56,320
if Gao Yayan

104
00:04:56,320 --> 00:04:58,000
really thought this tricycle
was meaningful to her,

105
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:59,960
why couldn't she tolerate Song Yanfei

106
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:01,220
keeping it in the yard,

107
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:02,760
leaving it on the roadside instead?

108
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:04,560
Was it really just
because it was in the way?

109
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:05,040
Right,

110
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:07,380
that's exactly what I just asked her.

111
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:08,480
Why would she buy back

112
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:09,800
the tricycle we processed

113
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:11,200
at a high price?

114
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:11,800
Exactly.

115
00:05:11,800 --> 00:05:13,520
Come here, major discovery.

116
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:14,120
Wei,

117
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:15,890
you stayed up all night?

118
00:05:16,080 --> 00:05:16,880
Have a bite.

119
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:18,120
Thanks, Wei.

120
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:19,780
Thank you, Wei.

121
00:05:24,120 --> 00:05:27,120
Do you remember the unresolved question

122
00:05:27,360 --> 00:05:29,620
that kept us from closing Xiao Ze's case?

123
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:32,159
The hemp rope.

124
00:05:33,360 --> 00:05:35,760
Do you remember
what Shen Xi said back then?

125
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:37,580
I didn't expect it.

126
00:05:37,840 --> 00:05:39,400
He picked up a rope from the ground

127
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:41,120
and quickly tied it to a tree.

128
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:42,600
He said if I didn't stay with him,

129
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:44,600
he would hang himself immediately.

130
00:05:44,840 --> 00:05:46,080
I was really scared.

131
00:05:47,440 --> 00:05:48,240
You said

132
00:05:48,360 --> 00:05:51,490
he picked up a rope from the ground
and tied it to the tree.

133
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:54,100
Where did that rope come from?

134
00:05:56,640 --> 00:05:57,440
I don't know.

135
00:05:58,800 --> 00:06:01,000
Where do you think the rope came from?

136
00:06:03,880 --> 00:06:04,880
I guess

137
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:07,480
he brought it with him.

138
00:06:08,400 --> 00:06:09,360
Because he asked me out

139
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:11,290
just to threaten me with his death.

140
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:13,400
So he must have prepared it himself.

141
00:06:16,920 --> 00:06:17,920
That makes sense.

142
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:20,520
Later, we checked
the surveillance footage.

143
00:06:20,520 --> 00:06:22,000
Indeed, there isn't.

144
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:22,600
Look,

145
00:06:23,040 --> 00:06:23,640
it's here.

146
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:25,680
He probably just got out of the car

147
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:27,740
and put the keys in his jacket pocket.

148
00:06:28,040 --> 00:06:30,120
Xiao Ze's shirt is slim-fit,

149
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:31,880
and he's holding his jacket.

150
00:06:33,520 --> 00:06:34,280
He put it on.

151
00:06:34,880 --> 00:06:36,080
There's no hemp rope.

152
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:38,520
Captain Weng,

153
00:06:39,760 --> 00:06:42,080
we'll have to rely on you
for the hemp rope clue.

154
00:06:42,080 --> 00:06:44,320
Every hardware store sells
this kind of hemp rope.

155
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:46,640
There's no difference
in material or workmanship.

156
00:06:46,640 --> 00:06:47,480
I think

157
00:06:47,680 --> 00:06:49,400
if we can't trace the source,

158
00:06:49,400 --> 00:06:51,200
we still have to figure out

159
00:06:51,640 --> 00:06:52,480
how this rope

160
00:06:52,680 --> 00:06:54,400
ended up in the woods.

161
00:06:56,120 --> 00:06:56,760
Shen Xi,

162
00:06:57,080 --> 00:06:59,040
are you sure it wasn't there
when you came in?

163
00:06:59,040 --> 00:06:59,920
Let me see.

164
00:07:09,760 --> 00:07:11,490
What's she holding in her hand?

165
00:07:12,080 --> 00:07:13,080
It's an envelope.

166
00:07:13,120 --> 00:07:14,080
Probably

167
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:16,240
the letter
Xiao Ze threatened her to write,

168
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:17,900
and that ticket or something.

169
00:07:18,960 --> 00:07:19,800
Captains,

170
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:21,240
I think

171
00:07:21,480 --> 00:07:22,280
the hemp rope

172
00:07:22,640 --> 00:07:24,480
is definitely the top priority

173
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:25,640
to investigate.

174
00:07:29,160 --> 00:07:31,480
Then we visited the neighborhood.

175
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:37,640
Hello, hello.

176
00:07:38,480 --> 00:07:39,640
Did you see anyone

177
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:40,640
carrying this kind of rope

178
00:07:40,640 --> 00:07:42,280
up the mountain?

179
00:07:42,760 --> 00:07:43,960
There's no firewood on the mountain.

180
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:45,159
What would they need the rope for?

181
00:07:45,159 --> 00:07:45,760
Sir,

182
00:07:46,280 --> 00:07:47,080
I'd like to ask

183
00:07:47,080 --> 00:07:48,680
if you've seen this hemp rope

184
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:49,640
around here.

185
00:07:50,840 --> 00:07:53,000
I haven't seen this hemp rope.

186
00:07:53,440 --> 00:07:54,720
Never seen it.

187
00:07:55,040 --> 00:07:56,640
Could you think about it again?

188
00:07:56,640 --> 00:07:57,100
This...

189
00:07:57,320 --> 00:07:58,180
just like this.

190
00:07:59,760 --> 00:08:00,760
Is it that one?

191
00:08:00,760 --> 00:08:02,800
The one the young man
used to hang himself?

192
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:04,120
What was he thinking?

193
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:05,280
Such a thick rope.

194
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:07,280
Thank you.

195
00:08:07,280 --> 00:08:08,600
I'll... I'll keep looking.

196
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:09,730
Thanks. No problem.

197
00:08:12,280 --> 00:08:14,210
Do you still remember this person?

198
00:08:14,680 --> 00:08:16,200
We only remember

199
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:17,640
the regulars who eat

200
00:08:17,640 --> 00:08:18,700
at our restaurant.

201
00:08:19,080 --> 00:08:20,280
We really didn't pay attention

202
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:21,360
to passersby.

203
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:23,480
Thank you.

204
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:24,490
You're welcome.

205
00:08:26,520 --> 00:08:27,480
And t-t-then...

206
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:29,080
I did send people to check

207
00:08:29,080 --> 00:08:31,720
all the hardware and agricultural
supply stores in the city,

208
00:08:31,720 --> 00:08:33,320
but we found no useful clues.

209
00:08:33,880 --> 00:08:34,480
Yeah.

210
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:36,559
Hasn't this clue

211
00:08:36,559 --> 00:08:38,690
basically been ruled out internally?

212
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:40,880
Wei,

213
00:08:41,280 --> 00:08:42,440
did you

214
00:08:42,720 --> 00:08:44,159
find something new?

215
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:45,960
Tell us.

216
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:47,240
Stop keeping me in suspense.

217
00:08:47,240 --> 00:08:48,640
Hurry up.

218
00:08:48,640 --> 00:08:49,960
How am I keeping you in suspense?

219
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:51,160
I later organized

220
00:08:51,160 --> 00:08:53,760
a carpet search of the area.

221
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:24,250
Captain Weng, look at that.

222
00:09:33,640 --> 00:09:35,280
A mini camera.

223
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:37,240
A camera.

224
00:09:37,720 --> 00:09:39,440
There's a camera in the tree.

225
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:41,000
Surprised?

226
00:09:41,640 --> 00:09:43,770
This was placed by our local TV station

227
00:09:44,560 --> 00:09:45,560
to shoot footage.

228
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:48,200
They are tracking the migration
of a migratory bird.

229
00:09:48,200 --> 00:09:49,080
Animal World.

230
00:09:49,480 --> 00:09:51,410
Pretty much. Something like that.

231
00:09:51,600 --> 00:09:53,000
The station said they placed

232
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:54,120
over a dozen around there.

233
00:09:54,120 --> 00:09:55,280
Over a dozen?

234
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:56,640
What about the angles?

235
00:09:56,640 --> 00:09:57,500
Are they clear?

236
00:09:59,760 --> 00:10:01,760
I actually found some useful clues

237
00:10:02,160 --> 00:10:02,920
in one of the cameras

238
00:10:02,920 --> 00:10:04,360
on the east side.

239
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:06,940
Lost it.

240
00:10:07,040 --> 00:10:08,120
Don't do this, Wei.

241
00:10:08,120 --> 00:10:10,000
Please look for it again.

242
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:11,320
No.

243
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:12,680
Y-Y-You...

244
00:10:13,240 --> 00:10:14,080
Where is it?

245
00:10:14,640 --> 00:10:17,100
I just love seeing you
look so disappointed.

246
00:10:17,360 --> 00:10:18,240
Thank you, Wei.

247
00:10:18,720 --> 00:10:19,850
Come on, Captain Li.

248
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:20,920
Let's take a look.

249
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:22,320
The first one, right?

250
00:10:26,840 --> 00:10:28,120
It's too blurry.

251
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:29,720
We can't see anything.

252
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:31,600
But there's a silhouette here.

253
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:33,360
But it looks

254
00:10:33,600 --> 00:10:34,800
kind of weird.

255
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:36,600
Look.

256
00:10:37,560 --> 00:10:39,490
He climbed up from the east, right?

257
00:10:40,600 --> 00:10:42,800
So the front camera couldn't catch him.

258
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:45,120
It's blurry

259
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:46,160
because its focal length is set

260
00:10:46,160 --> 00:10:47,480
for shooting the bird's nest up close.

261
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:48,640
It's clear up close,

262
00:10:48,680 --> 00:10:50,000
but blurry from a distance.

263
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,600
Then... is there a clear one?

264
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:52,560
Next clip.

265
00:10:58,120 --> 00:10:59,000
Why does this guy

266
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:01,280
look like a time traveler?

267
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:02,120
Who is this?

268
00:11:02,760 --> 00:11:03,600
An actor?

269
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:05,570
You don't get it, do you?

270
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:07,560
Wei definitely had someone

271
00:11:07,560 --> 00:11:08,800
run a technical analysis.

272
00:11:08,800 --> 00:11:09,360
Right?

273
00:11:10,160 --> 00:11:11,960
Next clip, technical analysis.

274
00:11:14,960 --> 00:11:16,090
Zoom in on the waist.

275
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:20,660
A hemp rope.

276
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:21,760
That's a hemp rope.

277
00:11:21,760 --> 00:11:22,520
See it?

278
00:11:22,560 --> 00:11:24,160
From this, we can deduce that

279
00:11:24,240 --> 00:11:25,480
the day before Xiao Ze died,

280
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:27,880
this person tied the rope
around his waist,

281
00:11:28,280 --> 00:11:29,880
crawled into the woods from the east,

282
00:11:29,880 --> 00:11:31,080
and threw the rope in.

283
00:12:01,560 --> 00:12:02,480
That's it?

284
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:03,280
That's it.

285
00:12:04,080 --> 00:12:06,080
What about the face? Who is this guy?

286
00:12:06,920 --> 00:12:07,680
Ask Captain Li.

287
00:12:07,680 --> 00:12:08,880
Captain Li, who is it?

288
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:11,120
Ancient costume.

289
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:13,120
Actor.

290
00:12:14,120 --> 00:12:14,850
Time travel.

291
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:16,600
Cosplay.

292
00:12:17,440 --> 00:12:18,520
Bai Xiaosi.

293
00:12:22,160 --> 00:12:23,000
Just my luck.

294
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:25,220
I've been hounded by you cops lately.

295
00:12:29,760 --> 00:12:31,020
Where is your grandma?

296
00:12:31,040 --> 00:12:33,040
My grandpa took her out for some sun.

297
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:34,960
Why are you guys here again?

298
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:36,200
Ask yourself.

299
00:12:36,200 --> 00:12:36,960
Bai Xiaosi,

300
00:12:37,600 --> 00:12:40,530
where were you at 11:00 p.m.
on the 16th of last month?

301
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:43,000
How could I remember that?

302
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:44,560
I've been locked up twice

303
00:12:44,560 --> 00:12:46,080
and detained for 15 days.

304
00:12:46,840 --> 00:12:48,240
Let me help you remember.

305
00:12:48,280 --> 00:12:49,080
Show it to him.

306
00:12:51,160 --> 00:12:52,420
Still can't remember?

307
00:12:56,560 --> 00:12:57,620
This is you, right?

308
00:12:59,640 --> 00:13:00,360
It's me.

309
00:13:00,600 --> 00:13:02,320
This video is from a year ago.

310
00:13:02,760 --> 00:13:04,320
It has nothing to do with the 16th.

311
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:04,920
Continue.

312
00:13:10,680 --> 00:13:12,210
Look at these three photos.

313
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:15,240
They must have something to do with you.

314
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:16,480
These have even less to do with me.

315
00:13:16,480 --> 00:13:18,010
You can't even see the face.

316
00:13:18,040 --> 00:13:19,480
What does this prove?

317
00:13:21,040 --> 00:13:23,570
Looks like Song Yanfei
was telling the truth.

318
00:13:23,720 --> 00:13:24,720
This kid did it.

319
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:26,200
It has nothing to do with Song Yanfei.

320
00:13:26,200 --> 00:13:27,460
Then let's arrest him.

321
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:29,960
Wait...

322
00:13:30,120 --> 00:13:32,650
What did Song Yanfei say
to make you arrest me?

323
00:13:32,720 --> 00:13:34,720
Song Yanfei has confessed
everything to us.

324
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:35,320
He said

325
00:13:35,640 --> 00:13:36,680
you were the one who killed them.

326
00:13:36,680 --> 00:13:37,080
Take him away.

327
00:13:37,080 --> 00:13:38,410
He's talking nonsense.

328
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:39,400
I didn't.

329
00:13:39,560 --> 00:13:41,420
So you do know Song Yanfei, right?

330
00:13:51,200 --> 00:13:52,520
Did you memorize my number?

331
00:13:52,520 --> 00:13:53,880
Let's grab a bite sometime.

332
00:13:53,880 --> 00:13:55,360
Yeah, I got it.

333
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:56,960
I'll call you when I get back.

334
00:13:58,040 --> 00:13:58,360
By the way,

335
00:13:58,360 --> 00:14:00,090
is anyone coming to pick you up?

336
00:14:00,400 --> 00:14:01,360
Probably not.

337
00:14:01,560 --> 00:14:03,240
My grandpa is taking care of my grandma.

338
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:04,240
My dad is dead,

339
00:14:04,440 --> 00:14:06,170
and my mom ran off with someone.

340
00:14:06,720 --> 00:14:08,680
I thought I had it the worst,

341
00:14:08,760 --> 00:14:10,220
but you're even worse off.

342
00:14:10,640 --> 00:14:11,440
Xiao Si.

343
00:14:12,920 --> 00:14:14,120
Is that your brother?

344
00:14:14,680 --> 00:14:15,160
I don't

345
00:14:15,320 --> 00:14:16,250
really know him.

346
00:14:16,640 --> 00:14:19,170
Alright, let's keep in touch
when we get back.

347
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:26,480
What are you doing?

348
00:14:26,480 --> 00:14:27,610
I need to talk to you.

349
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:28,210
Let's go.

350
00:14:28,360 --> 00:14:29,560
The car is over there.

351
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:31,120
Why should I go with you?

352
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:33,250
Haven't you caused me enough trouble?

353
00:14:33,960 --> 00:14:35,920
You don't recognize me
after getting out of jail?

354
00:14:35,920 --> 00:14:36,920
Wanna go back in?

355
00:14:38,640 --> 00:14:40,080
Treat me to a big meal,

356
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:41,770
and maybe I'll forgive you.

357
00:14:42,080 --> 00:14:42,920
Is that all you want?

358
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:43,450
Let's go.

359
00:14:43,720 --> 00:14:45,650
Pick any good restaurant you like.

360
00:14:48,400 --> 00:14:49,320
You smell...

361
00:14:49,560 --> 00:14:50,820
Go take a shower first.

362
00:14:54,360 --> 00:14:55,160
These 15 days

363
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:55,980
have really

364
00:14:56,080 --> 00:14:57,600
drained me dry.

365
00:14:58,920 --> 00:14:59,480
How is it?

366
00:14:59,880 --> 00:15:01,160
Feeling a bit recovered?

367
00:15:01,160 --> 00:15:02,080
Not bad.

368
00:15:04,520 --> 00:15:05,440
We're even now.

369
00:15:06,520 --> 00:15:07,780
Let's leave it at that.

370
00:15:08,440 --> 00:15:09,640
You're not afraid...

371
00:15:11,240 --> 00:15:12,320
Afraid of what?

372
00:15:12,560 --> 00:15:13,820
That you'll rat me out?

373
00:15:14,960 --> 00:15:15,560
Impossible.

374
00:15:15,560 --> 00:15:17,200
We're in the same boat now.

375
00:15:17,680 --> 00:15:19,010
You're not that stupid.

376
00:15:19,320 --> 00:15:20,000
Also,

377
00:15:20,320 --> 00:15:21,360
about Xiao Ze,

378
00:15:21,360 --> 00:15:22,560
I didn't do anything.

379
00:15:22,960 --> 00:15:24,080
I just threw a hemp rope,

380
00:15:24,080 --> 00:15:26,080
and it was in the middle of the night.

381
00:15:28,440 --> 00:15:30,400
We still need to get our stories
straight for the police,

382
00:15:30,400 --> 00:15:31,600
right?

383
00:15:32,760 --> 00:15:34,890
What if the police trace it back to you?

384
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:37,400
Can they really trace it?

385
00:15:40,640 --> 00:15:42,300
I'll just deny it completely.

386
00:15:42,680 --> 00:15:43,940
Deny what completely?

387
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:45,880
Deny that I went to the woods,

388
00:15:45,880 --> 00:15:47,560
and deny that I threw the rope.

389
00:15:54,560 --> 00:15:56,040
So you want me to admit it?

390
00:15:56,800 --> 00:15:58,800
If the police really trace it to you,

391
00:15:58,800 --> 00:16:00,530
it means they have CCTV footage

392
00:16:00,760 --> 00:16:01,800
or witnesses.

393
00:16:02,360 --> 00:16:03,440
Witnesses can be denied.

394
00:16:03,440 --> 00:16:04,840
But if it's CCTV footage,

395
00:16:05,120 --> 00:16:06,120
we're in trouble.

396
00:16:07,280 --> 00:16:09,080
But none of that is important right now.

397
00:16:09,080 --> 00:16:10,210
What's important is

398
00:16:10,480 --> 00:16:12,480
that we don't know each other at all.

399
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:14,320
I get it.

400
00:16:14,880 --> 00:16:17,810
The first thing I'll deny
to the death is knowing you.

401
00:16:22,040 --> 00:16:24,120
As long as you completely deny
that we know each other,

402
00:16:24,120 --> 00:16:26,360
even if the police have solid evidence,

403
00:16:26,400 --> 00:16:28,400
you can make up a reasonable excuse.

404
00:16:28,480 --> 00:16:29,200
Just say,

405
00:16:29,720 --> 00:16:31,520
"I wanted to experience
a martial arts movie,

406
00:16:31,520 --> 00:16:33,600
so I wore a costume into the woods."

407
00:16:34,280 --> 00:16:35,600
"The hemp rope around my waist

408
00:16:35,600 --> 00:16:36,800
was just a decoration."

409
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:38,360
"I didn't think it looked good
when I left,

410
00:16:38,360 --> 00:16:40,690
and it was worthless,
so I threw it there."

411
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:41,720
That way,

412
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:42,860
even if they ask...

413
00:16:43,120 --> 00:16:44,180
It doesn't matter.

414
00:16:46,160 --> 00:16:47,040
Expert.

415
00:16:50,280 --> 00:16:51,200
Xiaosi,

416
00:16:52,440 --> 00:16:53,680
you've lied to the police

417
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:55,800
time and time again

418
00:16:56,280 --> 00:16:58,480
and deliberately concealed the truth.

419
00:16:58,920 --> 00:17:00,120
You're suspected of a crime,

420
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:00,760
you know?

421
00:17:02,880 --> 00:17:03,840
This is

422
00:17:04,240 --> 00:17:05,119
a major case.

423
00:17:05,599 --> 00:17:07,329
It involves more than one life.

424
00:17:07,640 --> 00:17:08,400
Will lying

425
00:17:08,599 --> 00:17:10,000
solve anything?

426
00:17:12,400 --> 00:17:14,000
Then ask whatever you want

427
00:17:14,240 --> 00:17:14,920
to know.

428
00:17:15,640 --> 00:17:16,880
What is your relationship
with Xiao Ze, Shen Xi,

429
00:17:16,880 --> 00:17:17,880
Song Yanfei,

430
00:17:18,200 --> 00:17:19,040
and Gao Yayan?

431
00:17:19,040 --> 00:17:19,839
How did you meet them?

432
00:17:19,839 --> 00:17:20,640
One at a time.

433
00:17:26,520 --> 00:17:27,680
You all know about

434
00:17:28,480 --> 00:17:29,280
Xiao Ze and me.

435
00:17:29,280 --> 00:17:30,340
I already told you.

436
00:17:31,040 --> 00:17:32,900
I'm not hiding anything anymore.

437
00:17:33,560 --> 00:17:34,040
No.

438
00:17:34,560 --> 00:17:34,920
Okay.

439
00:17:35,400 --> 00:17:36,460
What about Shen Xi?

440
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:38,280
Are you hiding anything?

441
00:17:39,200 --> 00:17:39,800
Yes.

442
00:17:40,280 --> 00:17:42,560
The part about her hiring me as a driver

443
00:17:43,080 --> 00:17:43,740
was made up.

444
00:17:44,040 --> 00:17:46,640
Song Yanfei actually
introduced me to the job.

445
00:17:52,800 --> 00:17:54,120
Then let's talk about

446
00:17:54,640 --> 00:17:56,280
how you met Song Yanfei.
